                "quote": "let renewalRefusal (today: DateOnly) (loan: Loan) (library: Library) : LendingError option ="
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 221,
                "quote": "| LoanOverdue _ -> \"overdue\""
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The renewal rule (overdue, then limit, then holds, in the decision's order) is decided once in Tier 2 by `renewalRefusal`. `Loans.renew` uses it, and so do the `loans` view (`ofLoan`) and `renewAll`. Tier 3 only maps an error value to display text, and `renewAll` only loops and calls `Loans.renew`. The CLI now calls the `UseCases.renew` use case. Before, it loaded the store and called `Loans.renew` directly, so this removes an existing Tier 4 re-entry into Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/UseCases.fs",
                "line": 101,
                "quote": "query ports (Views.memberLoans (ports.Clock()) (MemberId memberId))"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The clock is read through the `Clock` port. `renew` and `renewAll` go through `commit`, which uses the Store port. The CLI no longer calls `ports.Store.Load` or `Save` itself. The new Tier 2 function is pure and the `Ports` record is unchanged.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-03": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Application/Views.fs",
                "line": 243,
                "quote": "MaxRenewals = Policy.renewLimit"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The limit is `Policy.renewLimit`, read in `renewalRefusal` and in `ofRenew`. The refusal order lives only in `renewalRefusal`. The `renewed N of M times` text takes its limit from the error value, not from a second constant.",
            "score": 2
          }
        },
        "2": {
          "ARC-REV-01": {
            "evidence": [
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Loans.fs",
                "line": 65,
                "quote": "let renewLimitOf (loan: Loan) (library: Library) : int ="
              },
              {
                "file": "src/Lending.Transition/Policy.fs",
                "line": 22,
                "quote": "let renewLimit memberType ="
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The limit by member type (standard 2, student 1, staff 4) is a policy value in Tier 2. `renewLimitOf` finds the borrower and applies it. Tier 3 and Tier 4 only call `Loans.renewLimitOf` (in `ofRenew`) or read the limit from the error value. No member-type branching was added above Tier 2.",
            "score": 2
          },
          "ARC-REV-02": {
            "evidence": [],
            "rationale": "The change adds no effects. `renewLimitOf` and `Policy.renewLimit` are pure. The existing clock and store ports are used unchanged.",
